-- Week 48 — The Quality of Everyday Encounters
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET
  weekly_theme        = $cw48_theme$The Quality of Everyday Encounters$cw48_theme$,
  the_territory       = $cw48_terr$Improving the quality of contact without managing somebody else's mood.$cw48_terr$,
  opening_question    = $cw48_oq$What behaviour from another person makes you feel taken seriously?$cw48_oq$,
  week_type           = $cw48_wt$Standard$cw48_wt$,
  reflective_question = $cw48_rq$Complete:
In  relationship, I will practise  because it communicates . I will judge the practice by whether I did it respectfully, not by whether I changed their mood.$cw48_rq$,
  interactive_activity = $cw48_ia$RESPONSIVENESS LAB — 20 minutes
Practise four micro-behaviours with fictional/neutral topics:
1. LISTEN-BACK: “What I hear you saying is…”
2. FOLLOW-UP: ask one question that directly follows what was said.
3. SPECIFIC APPRECIATION: name behaviour + effect, with no appearance praise.
4. RELIABILITY PLAN: convert “we should catch up” or “I'll help sometime” into a realistic specific commitment — or decline honestly.
Then choose one behaviour to test this week.
OUTCOME-RELEASE DRILL
Read scenarios where someone uses good relational behaviour but the other person remains upset or declines the interaction. Ask: What was within their control? What was not?$cw48_ia$,
  kids_picture_book   = $cw48_bk$Each Kindness$cw48_bk$,
  kids_picture_book_author = $cw48_bka$Jacqueline Woodson$cw48_bka$,
  kids_picture_book_note = $cw48_bkn$WHY IT FITS: It can support noticing everyday choices without teaching children that every action creates a magical ripple or that they control other people's feelings.$cw48_bkn$,
  kids_picture_book_question = $cw48_bkq$What does someone do that helps you know they are listening?$cw48_bkq$,
  kids_game = $cw48_g$REMEMBER & RESPOND
In pairs, Child A says one safe, ordinary fact: favourite game, pet, colour, hobby, something they did on the weekend. Child B asks one follow-up question. Later in the session, B tries to remember the fact.
Swap.$cw48_g$,
  kids_game_under5 = $cw48_g5$Use simple picture choices and one follow-up: “Which one do you like?”$cw48_g5$,
  kids_parent_handout = $cw48_ph$Prompt:
- “What did they say?”
- “What could you ask next?”
- “What can you thank them for specifically?”
- “Did they want space?”
And remind children: you can care without fixing the feeling.$cw48_ph$,
