-- Week 52 — Ending Well — Review, Ownership and Choice
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET
  weekly_theme        = $cw52_theme$Ending Well — Review, Ownership and Choice$cw52_theme$,
  the_territory       = $cw52_terr$Finishing the programme without needing to turn the ending into another beginning.$cw52_terr$,
  opening_question    = $cw52_oq$What is one concrete thing you can do, notice or explain now that was less available to you before? “Nothing major” is a valid answer.$cw52_oq$,
  week_type           = $cw52_wt$Integration$cw52_wt$,
  reflective_question = $cw52_rq$Write:
This year I used . I learned . I am leaving . I am keeping . The programme is complete, and what happens next is my choice.$cw52_rq$,
  interactive_activity = $cw52_ia$THE EVIDENCE-BASED YEAR REVIEW — 25 minutes
Choose up to four moments from the year and complete:
1. WHAT I REMEMBER: …
2. WHAT I DID WITH IT: …
3. WHAT HAPPENED NEXT: …
4. WHAT I CAN REASONABLY CONCLUDE: …
5. WHAT I CANNOT CONCLUDE: …
Then write your exit line:
- “I am keeping…”
- “I am leaving…”
- “I am curious about…”
No future commitment is required.
OPTIONAL ACKNOWLEDGMENT
Give each participant three choices:
- share one sentence;
- place a private written card in their own envelope to take home;
- pass completely.
No silent “witnessing” protocol, applause hierarchy or facilitator interpretation. A simple “thank you” follows any share.
PROGRAMME HAND-BACK
Facilitator reads:
“This curriculum is complete. You do not owe Mindcast an ongoing practice, a transformation story, continued attendance, contact with this group, or agreement with what was taught. Keep what is useful, challenge or discard what is not, and use other people, communities and professional supports where they fit better. If you choose to engage with Mindcast again, that is a new choice — not an obligation created by completing this year.”$cw52_ia$,
  kids_picture_book   = $cw52_bk$The Goodbye Book$cw52_bk$,
  kids_picture_book_author = $cw52_bka$Todd Parr$cw52_bka$,
  kids_picture_book_note = $cw52_bkn$another approved, age-appropriate book about endings and mixed feelings.
WHY IT FITS: The goal is to normalise endings rather than telling children every ending is secretly a new beginning or an adventure that must continue.$cw52_bkn$,
  kids_picture_book_question = $cw52_bkq$What is one thing you remember from this year that was useful or fun?$cw52_bkq$,
  kids_game = $cw52_g$CHOOSE YOUR THREE STATIONS
Set up a small trail with 6–8 neutral picture/object stations representing tools from the year. Each child chooses up to three to visit. At each they may say:
- “I remember this.”
- “I used this.”
- “I don't want this one.”
- “I want to keep this.”
They do not have to complete the whole trail.$cw52_g$,
  kids_game_under5 = $cw52_g5$Offer three picture stations and let the child choose one, two, three or none with a caregiver/facilitator nearby.$cw52_g5$,
  kids_parent_handout = $cw52_ph$Tell caregivers explicitly:
- the 52-week curriculum is complete;
- no Mindcast homework continues;
- use tools only if the child finds them helpful;
- do not treat continued attendance as necessary for maintaining progress;
- ordinary family, school, healthcare and community supports remain primary.$cw52_ph$,
