  theme_title            = $s52c_tt$Ending Well — Review, Ownership and Choice$s52c_tt$,
  heavy_week_flag        = false,
  s5_source_opening_hook = $s52c_hk$Some things end: school terms, sports seasons, books, visits and programmes. An ending does not mean something went wrong. Today Mindcast's 52-week programme ends too.$s52c_hk$,
  s5_source_core_concept = $s52c_cc$Today is a celebration and a goodbye.
Children do not have to say they changed. They do not have to read a letter, thank the programme, make a promise or keep practising.
They can choose:
REMEMBER → KEEP SOME → LEAVE SOME → SAY GOODBYE.$s52c_cc$,
  core_concept           = $s52c_cco$A healthy ending helps children remember what they learned, choose what is useful, say goodbye without pressure, and understand that they do not need to keep attending or keep practising in order to be okay or keep growing.
Child translation: We can celebrate finishing, keep a few useful tools, leave some things behind, and say goodbye.$s52c_cco$,
  teaching_points        = $s52c_tp$1. Finishing is enough. You completed the year. You do not have to prove you became a better, braver or different person.
2. You can remember different things from other children. There is no right favourite lesson or tool.
3. You can leave tools behind. Something can have been fun once and not be something you want to keep using.
4. You do not have to share private reflections. You can say “pass” during the final session without explaining why.
5. Different feelings about goodbye are okay. Happy, sad, relieved, excited, unsure or not bothered are all allowed.
6. Friends can stay friends if families choose, but nobody has to stay connected to the group. Mindcast does not call the group a family or promise “forever.”
7. Your caregivers and normal communities still matter most. Family/whānau, school, friends, clubs, culture and trusted adults continue outside the programme.
8. The tools do not belong to Mindcast. You can use an idea in your own words, forget it, find another way, or ask a grown-up for something better.$s52c_tp$,
  signal_metaphor        = $s52c_sm$Finishing a book does not mean the book follows you around asking you to reread it. You can remember a favourite page and still put the book back on the shelf.$s52c_sm$,
  private_write_prompt   = $s52c_pw$Draw three boxes:
- I WANT TO REMEMBER
- I AM HAPPY TO LEAVE HERE
- A GROWN-UP I CAN ASK FOR HELP
Children may leave any box blank.$s52c_pw$,
  experiential_exercise  = $s52c_ex$MY END-OF-YEAR TAKE-HOME CARD — 15 minutes
Children choose:
1. up to three tools/ideas to draw on the front;
2. one trusted-adult/help reminder on the back;
3. one optional goodbye sentence:
There is no “something I gave,” no ongoing commitment, no collective oath and no requirement to praise another child.
OPTIONAL GROUP MOMENT
Go around once with three options:
- name one thing you want to keep;
- name one thing you enjoyed;
- say “pass.”
Every response gets the same “thank you.”
Do not require appreciation of peers or facilitators.
PROGRAMME HAND-BACK
Facilitator reads:
“Today this Mindcast programme is finished. You do not have to keep practising Mindcast things, keep coming here, or tell us that it changed you. Some tools may help later and some may not. Your family, whānau, teachers, friends and trusted grown-ups are still there when you need help. You get to take what was useful and leave the rest.”$s52c_ex$,
  guided_reflection      = $s52c_gr$What do you want to remember?
What are you happy to finish?
Which tools are yours to use only when you want them?
Which grown-ups can help with bigger problems?
How do you feel about saying goodbye today?
Whatever answer you have is okay.$s52c_gr$,
  journaling_prompt      = $s52c_jp$Finish or draw:
I am keeping . I am leaving . I can ask  for help. Mindcast is finished, and that is okay.$s52c_jp$,
  intention_prompt       = $s52c_ip$There is no required intention after the programme.$s52c_ip$,
  core_affirmation       = $s52c_ca$I can keep what helped me and leave the rest. I can say goodbye, and I have trusted people and places outside Mindcast too.$s52c_ca$,
